From: Batocera 15kHz CRT on Intel gen9
Subject: [PATCH] drm/i915: don't advertise Y/Yf tiled scanout on gen9

The display engine refuses Y/Yf tiled scanout while a pipe runs in IF-ID
interlace mode -- see the "Y/Yf tiling not supported in IF-ID mode" check in
skl_plane_check() (drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/skl_universal_plane.c).

Userspace picks a framebuffer modifier when it allocates the buffer, long
before any mode is set, and Mesa/glamor prefers Y tiling for scanout on gen9.
The result is that every interlaced modeset fails the atomic check with
-EINVAL, which userspace reports as:

    xrandr: Configure crtc 0 failed
    (EE) modeset(0): failed to set mode: No such file or directory

This makes real 480i impossible on a 15kHz CRT even though the hardware
supports interlace on this generation (intel_dp.c already sets
interlace_allowed for DISPLAY_VER < 12).

Only advertise LINEAR/X_TILED on gen9 so that the scanout buffer is
interlace capable from the moment it is allocated. X tiling is a first
class scanout format here, so glamor acceleration keeps working.

Note the alternative of forcing linear buffers with Option "AccelMethod"
"none" in xorg.conf does work for interlace, but Batocera's Mesa has no
swrast_dri.so, so EmulationStation loses GL and crash-loops.

Tested on Intel HD Graphics 530 (Skylake, DISPLAY_VER 9) driving a
consumer CRT TV over DisplayPort -> VGA -> SCART, kernel 6.18.16.
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_fb.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_fb.c
@@ -556,6 +556,23 @@
 		return false;
 
 	/*
+	 * batocera-15khz: the display engine rejects Y/Yf tiled scanout (and the
+	 * CCS variants, which are Y based) in IF-ID interlace mode, see the
+	 * "Y/Yf tiling not supported in IF-ID mode" check in skl_plane_check().
+	 * Userspace picks a modifier at buffer allocation time, long before any
+	 * interlaced mode is set, and gen9 Mesa/glamor prefers Y tiling, which
+	 * then makes every interlaced modeset fail with -EINVAL. Only advertise
+	 * LINEAR/X_TILED on gen9 so the scanout buffer is interlace capable from
+	 * the start; X tiling is a first class scanout format here, so glamor
+	 * acceleration keeps working (unlike AccelMethod "none", which has no
+	 * swrast fallback on this build and breaks EmulationStation).
+	 */
+	if (DISPLAY_VER(display) == 9 &&
+	    md->modifier != DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR &&
+	    md->modifier != I915_FORMAT_MOD_X_TILED)
+		return false;
+
+	/*
 	 * Separate AuxCCS and Flat CCS modifiers to be run only on platforms
 	 * where supported.
 	 */
